&gt; :dna: *Apply to the <http://aixbiosecurity.com|AIxBiosecurity Research Fellowship>* (Apply <https://airtable.com/appdHmLGlAlIVkA8A/pagTn8kHWFL3Q4sHx/form|here>)
&gt; 
&gt; <http://erafellowship.org/|ERA>, in partnership with the <https://www.cambiohub.org/|Cambridge Biosecurity Hub>, is accepting applications for our 10-week, full-time <https://www.aixbiosecurity.com/|AIxBiosecurity fellowship>. This fully funded programme equips researchers and entrepreneurs to investigate ways to reduce extreme risks from engineered and natural biological threats amid rapidly advancing biotechnology and emerging AI capabilities.
&gt; 
&gt; *The deadline to apply is October 19th, 23:59 UTC.*
&gt; 
&gt; Fellows on our programme will be supported by expert mentors, dedicated research managers and a series of speaker events, workshops and networking sessions. Past mentors have worked at organisations like *SecureBio, CLTR, University of Oxford, Global Biofutures, RAND, ARIA, Fourth Eon Bio, and more.* The programme will support fellows *across three tracks: the research track, placement track, and founding track*—with the opportunity of receiving 6+ months extension or incubation funding.
&gt; 
&gt; Key details at a glance:
&gt; • Duration: 10 weeks full-time, during 18th January - 26th March
&gt; • Location: Cambridge, UK
&gt; • Stipend: £10,000
&gt; • Structure: every fellow will be paired with a research manager &amp; mentor
&gt; 
&gt; Whether you're coming from an AI, biology, policy or founding background, we hope you strongly consider applying! If you have any questions, you can contact us at <mailto:hello@erafellowship.org|hello@erafellowship.org>

