Cool post I saw on bluedot slack:
&gt; *`AI Safety for Builders: micro fellowship | Call for Mentors`*
&gt; 
&gt; If we take AI progress and its implications seriously - ensuring AI goes well means automating a lot of AI safety work. Which means building more of AI safety tools, infrastructures, pipelines, etc.
&gt; 
&gt; This is right now under-served. While a bunch of fellowships and research orgs exists to steer AI safety research, relatively less is done in building AI safety tools.
&gt; 
&gt; To counter this - *we recently raised a grant to pilot a AI Safety for Builders micro fellowship. A ~4 weeks sprint to build AI Safety tools*. (If this is done well, we plan to scale up soon).
&gt; ..
&gt; 
&gt; This is an expression of interest call for mentors. Do you have a tool-shaped AI safety idea you want to get build? (or you can see an example list in the website).
&gt; 
&gt; *An ideal mentor will have a strong builder or product background, and likely some AI safety context too*.
&gt; 
&gt; Please fill the embedded form to share your expression of interest. Feel free to ask questions / share feedback.
&gt; 
&gt; <https://aisafety.builders/?s=1|aisafety.builders/?s=1>

